{"title":"What should I ask Richard Hanania?","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/957391955/0/marginalrevolution~What-should-I-ask-Richard-Hanania.html","date":1779923240000,"content":"<p>Yes, I will be doing a Conversation with him.  Richard does have a new book coming out, <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Kakistocracy-Why-Populism-Ends-Disaster/dp/0063479990/ref=sr_1_1?crid=2WGK2QB3J2XKV&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.qg9YGCdjGaUX2UTiGrrMdiExbpNzgHL1VFNsGBMWQo1n35b0m_w1TC2XnumEf8Nrv_owTkWqh1Kc3LjdmLParZiVn6s0R0tHP5klRWKVt7c.ifmvDfjB7K_QAPohY9I47WoTBwC-6fh0dtuT_x9Qg9Q&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=richard+hanania&amp;qid=1779923071&amp;sprefix=richard+hanania%2Caps%2C336&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">Kakistocracy: Why Populism Ends in Disaster</a>.  While I liked the book (and blurbed it), I do not feel our conversation about the book would be that interesting — too much beating up on the stupidities of other people, which is an activity not in short supply.  So we agreed to (mostly) discuss Joseph Conrad’s <em>Nostromo</em> instead.  Given that, what should I ask Richard?</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/05/what-should-i-ask-richard-hanania.html\">What should I ask Richard Hanania?</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/957391955/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/957391955/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/957391955/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/957391955/marginalrevolutio